# rule.forbid.native-memory

**never persist knowledge into claude's native memory** (`~/.claude/**/memory/`, `~/.claude/**/MEMORY.md`). capture it durably in this repo instead:

- **lessons** → briefs in `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/`
- **tactics** → skills in `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/skills/`

⇒ the instinct to persist is *good* — keep it. only the destination is wrong.

## .why

native memory is **machine-local** (lives in `~/.claude/`, never leaves this laptop) · **invisible in git** (no diff, no review, no history) · **not reusable** (the next traveler — human or clone, any machine — never sees it) · **not durable** (one wipe and the lesson is gone).

durable capture in `.agent/` is the opposite: git-visible, reviewed in PRs, booted into every future session — so a lesson hardwon once is never won twice.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a concept surprised you or was hard to discover | a **brief** |
| a rule, gotcha, or fix is worth a note | a **brief** |
| you built a repeatable command or workflow | a **skill** |
| you feel the urge to *"remember this"* | 🔴 that urge IS the cue. redirect it |

a PreToolUse hook (`memory.guard`) halts writes to native memory and prints this redirect — so you need not recall the rule mid-flow.

## 🟡 .the exception — GENERALIZE machine-local paths and secrets

some notes carry literals that must not enter a shared repo verbatim: local absolute paths · secrets and secret-hints · per-clone scratch. **the lesson is still worth capture — the literal is the only problem.**

- 👎 `keyrack for this host lives at /home/vlad/.rhachet/keyrack/ehmpath.json`
- 👍 `keyrack lives at ~/.rhachet/keyrack/<owner>.json`

for a **true secret** (a credential value, token, key), do not even generalize the value — capture only the **shape** of the lesson (*"unlock the keyrack before integration tests"*), never the secret.

## .what is allowed

`~/.claude/settings.json` and other **config** (not memory) · `CLAUDE.md` (already durable + git-visible) · **reads** of native memory — only *writes* are halted.

🟡 **the guard is a safety net, not a seal.** it cannot catch every path, so do not read its silence as approval. the discipline is yours.

blocker: a write to `~/.claude/**/memory/**` or `~/.claude/**/MEMORY.md`.

> the diary fades; the noticeboard endures. write where the next traveler will read. 🦉📜
